      "textEn": "618\n\n“Oh, son of Pritha, Arjuna! Now you listen to how, by practicing yoga with my complete consciousness and by making the mind\nattached to me, you can understand me completely without doubt.\"Krishna and his\nOnly by having unwavering faith in the teachings can reality be understood (Asanshayam Samagam\nMam). Man can also know how Krishna's physical and spiritual powers are\nworking. How they are present everywhere, although every object is not in them. This\nis the complete philosophy of the Vaishnavas, Achintya Bhedabheda Darshan. Every object is emanated from Krishna, but this does not mean that every object should be worshiped. Mental contemplation (knowledge) does not tell us reality in the same\nform, it remains incomplete. So-called scientists try to prove that\nGod does not exist, and every event occurs due to the laws of nature, but this is incomplete knowledge, because\nUntil God directs, no object can function.\nIts explanation is given by God himself in the Bhagavad Gita\n(9.10)—\n\nMayaadhyakshena Prakritih Sacharacharam. For this reason, O son of Kunti, the world is changing. “Hey Kunti's son! This physical nature works under my direction, and it produces all the moving and non-moving\nanimals. This creation is repeatedly born and destroyed according to its own rules.\nIt is.” In this context, Srila Madhvacharya's commentary is—Durghatatvatad arthatvena parameshwarenaiva kalpitam. Every\nobject's foundation is Lord Vasudeva. Vasudeva is everything, thus he is very rare among great souls. Only he can understand this as the same Mahatma,\nwho is fully knowledgeable. Such a Mahatma is rare. For the stars, for these meanings, even the shadow is not.\nNot a single element or defect is false. 59. Meaning of the word:\n\nKshiti-adinam—Of the five elements beginning with earth; Iha—In this world; Arthanaam—Of those five elements; Chhaya—Reflection; Na—Not; Katama—Which of these; Api—Undoubtedly; Hi—Indeed; Nishchaye—Certainly; Na—Not; San